<em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman has disputed the authenticity of iPhone Ultra renders shared by the usually reliable leaker Evan Blass on X (Twitter). The images show the unreleased foldable iPhone in not just the rumored space gray and white colors, but also in a <a href="https://x.com/_evanblass_/status/2092673524456415626?s=20">striking red</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/evan-blass-red-iphone-ultra-xiaomi.jpeg" alt="" width="1200" height="675" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1061375" /><br/>
"Hearing these renders came from Xiaomi," <a href="https://x.com/markgurman/status/2092695626383602176?s=20">wrote Gurman</a>, commenting on Blass's post. "This isn't a legitimate look at the foldable iPhone, which also doesn't come in red or green. Just renders made by Xiaomi for some reason. Carry on."<br/>
<br/>
Apple is said to be planning to "stay away from fun colors" and stick to more traditional space gray/black and silver/white finishes for the book-style foldable iPhone. One rumor has described the darker color as a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/05/11/foldable-iphone-to-launch-in-just-two-colors/">shade of indigo</a> rather than black. Another rumor suggests there <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/05/foldable-iphone-may-not-come-in-black/">might not be a black color</a> at all.<br/>
<br/>
